# Architecture VSA v2.1

Full docs: `docs/architecture/vsa.md` · `docs/architecture/guidelines.md`  
Module context: `src/App/Features/{Module}/AGENTS.md` is source of truth for that Feature folder.

## Layout

```
src/App/
├── Program.cs              # ≤40 lines — never edit per slice
├── Host/                   # HTTP cross-cutting only
├── Shared/                 # Kernel, Infrastructure, Platform
└── Features/{Module}/
    ├── AGENTS.md           # module context — read before editing
    ├── {Entity}.cs         # noun = domain + repo + EF config
    └── {Slice}.cs          # verb = Command + Validator + Handler + IEndpoint

tests/App.Tests/{Module}/{Slice}Tests.cs   # flat mirror (no Features/ prefix)
```

## New slice checklist

1. Read `src/App/Features/{Module}/AGENTS.md`
2. Create `src/App/Features/{Module}/{Slice}.cs`
3. Create `tests/App.Tests/{Module}/{Slice}Tests.cs`
4. Update `features.json` (app, test, route, featureFlag)
5. Update module `AGENTS.md` if public surface changed
6. Do NOT edit `Program.cs` — use `IEndpoint` auto-discovery

## Feature flags

- Constants: `App.Host.FeatureFlags`
- Gate endpoint: `.RequireFeature(FeatureFlags.X)`
- Config: `appsettings.json` → `FeatureFlags` section

## Module registration

Each module exposes `{Module}Module.cs`:

- `Add{Module}Module(this IServiceCollection)` — repos, providers, tenant filters
- `Add{Module}ModulePolicies(this AuthorizationOptions)` — RBAC (when applicable)

`Program.cs` calls `AddFeatureModules()` in `Host/Configurations/FeatureModulesConfiguration.cs`.

## Contracts

Cross-slice DTOs live in `{Module}Contracts.cs` (e.g. `AuthContracts.cs`, `TenantContracts.cs`).

## Repositories

Per-aggregate interfaces only — **no** generic `IRepository<T>` in public contracts.

| Layer | Location | Rule |
|-------|----------|------|
| Interface | `{Entity}.cs` | `I{Entity}Repository` — domain-specific methods only |
| Implementation | `{Entity}.cs` | `internal sealed class {Entity}Repository(AppDbContext db)` |
| Shared EF boilerplate | `Shared/EfRepositoryHelpers.cs` | `internal static` — `GetByIdAsync`, `AddAsync`, `Update` |

```csharp
// Delegate generic CRUD; keep domain queries in the repo
public Task<User?> GetByIdAsync(Guid id, CancellationToken ct = default) =>
    EfRepositoryHelpers.GetByIdAsync(db.Set<User>(), id, ct);

public Task<User?> GetByEmailAsync(string email, CancellationToken ct = default) =>
    db.Set<User>().FirstOrDefaultAsync(u => u.Email.Value == normalized, ct);
```

- Use `db.Set<T>()` — `AppDbContext` has no explicit `DbSet` properties.
- Tenant query filters: register `ITenantQueryFilterConfigurator` in `{Module}Module.cs`.
- Tests: call `TestServiceFactory.SetTenant(provider, tenantId)` before repo/handler resolution.

## Tests

- Unit/handler: `tests/App.Tests` + InMemory via `TestServiceFactory`; set tenant with `SetTenant` before resolve
- Architecture: `tests/ArchitectureTests` enforces slice layout — keep green on every slice add
- E2E: `tests/E2ETests` + `E2EWebApplicationFactory`; prefer HTTP contracts over internals
- Never put tests under `src/App/`

## Anti-patterns (never)

- Folders per layer (`Handlers/`, `Mappers/`, `Validators/`)
- Subfolder per slice (`RegisterUser/RegisterUser.cs`) — use flat file
- Tests inside `src/App/`
- Controllers monolithic per module
- `[Authorize]` without policy name
- Generic `IRepository<T>` or base repository class exposed outside `Shared/`

## Shared rules

- `Kernel.cs` / `Platform.cs` must NOT reference `App.Features.*`
- Slice file cap: ~150 lines — split endpoint if exceeded
